WEBVTT

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:39.200
Her Highness Ecarlate Juptris
 St. Piria has arrived!

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.080
Welcome.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.920
I am Mainess, the Chief of Protocol who

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.770
will be conducting the marital rites.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:51.090
Until the day of the wedding, 
I will also be taking care of you.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.900
And where's Jugglaburk?

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.460
He rode with us, but we haven't 
even been introduced.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.220
That is because it is the 
custom of this house that

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.540
the two will meet for the first 
time on the day of the ceremony,

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.430
once all of the eighteen wedding 
rituals have been completed.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.410
A custom, huh?

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:06.660
Man, that's strict.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.170
Sounds like the mother and 
sister-in-law will be pretty annoying.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.080
Cut it out already, Kon.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.010
You're so rude.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.270
I just wanted to meet 
that Jugglaburk person.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.820
There's something I want to ask him.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.950
These will be your quarters 
during the days of the rituals.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.650
If there is anything you need, 
please don't hesitate to—

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:30.210
Yes!

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.000
I want to go to Olvidia!

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.010
That is not a place 
where humans can go.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.140
I came here because I 
was told that if I came

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.310
to Jugglaburk's territory, 
I'd be able to go to the

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.700
floating city of Olvidia.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.640
That's why I wanted to meet 
him, to ask about that.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.310
There is a research group studying 
Olvidia here in the city...

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:51.820
That's it! Yeah!

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.420
I'm fine with that.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.060
So where are they?

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:55.860
That's a secret.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.860
What the hell?!

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.800
What is this, Area 51?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.980
Can't you just tell me, pretty please?

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:04.350
Rules are rules.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.390
Don't be such a stickler.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:07.910
It is my duty.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:08.770
Excuse me.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.420
Man, my last lead is gone!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.400
I thought it was going to 
be a straight shot there.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.090
Where did I go wrong?!

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.830
Just calm down.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.340
Why don't you take a bath?

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.260
I won't learn anything 
new by calming down!

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.340
Oh, is it that?

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.060
Where the story won't 
progress until you sleep?

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.640
Like, there will be new 
developments the next day?

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.390
The wedding rituals 
will start tomorrow.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.200
That's it!

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.780
Wait, no it isn't.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.580
I'll have to find another way.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.110
That's it, that's it!

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.720
Yeah, I'm really sorry.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.610
Yeah, let's sit down for a 
nice drink next time we meet.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.150
On me, on me.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.240
No problem, no problem. 
I mean you're doing me a favor.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:51.020
All right.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.740
Got it.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.110
I know.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:54.790
Know what?

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.540
Where the research center is.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:58.130
But how?

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:02.760
Well, I've come this far with you, 
I figured I'd see it through to the end.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.660
That's not what I mean.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.010
How did you find out?

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.770
You shouldn't underestimate my network.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.270
You mean ratwork?

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.070
You call that to question?!

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.600
You know, I just don't care anymore.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.610
So, where is the research center?

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:21.930
Right here.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.530
Here, huh?

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.200
What's written up there?

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.700
Ixion Research Center.

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:30.200
Ixion?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.700
Ixion.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.420
Ixion?

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:35.970
Wait, what?!

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.900
It's like I heard some 
voice saying "finally" or

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.380
"there we go" or "now 
we're getting to it."

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.970
Don't worry about it.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:47.180
However, it does say that you can't 
walk in here without permission.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:51.160
I may not have permission, 
but I won't be walking.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.390
I am crawling!

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.690
Same difference!

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.160
Welcome.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:04.860
How may I help you?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.740
You're acting so normal that 
you threw me for a loop!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.080
How may I help you?

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.910
Uh well, it would take 
too long to explain,

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.780
but maybe you could take me to 
someone who I could talk to?

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.860
What exactly do you 
wish to speak about?

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:22.710
Um well, I've been asked 
if I'm a Hyperion.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.640
And if I came from a place called 
Olvidia, well, actually it's Mitaka...

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.970
Anyway, it might be a 
place above the sky.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:32.090
And I'd like to know how to go there.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.040
Wh-What?!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.990
I'm not a suspicious person!

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.850
What evidence do you have 
that you are a Hyperion?

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.380
Hey, just a minute! 
What is this, an interrogation?

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.880
Don't think I don't know my rights.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.520
You came here because you 
want to know about Olvidia.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:09.780
That's right.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.290
Do you know anything about 
that city in the sky?

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.310
I am willing to exchange 
information with you, but first,

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.680
I will see evidence that 
you are a Hyperion.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.350
This is Alma Gear, right?

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.530
Well, I can use it.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.950
Anything else is 
circumstantial evidence.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.650
I fell from the sky.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.960
That means I'm not from this world.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.370
I'm from a place called Shimorenjaku, 
 Mitaka city, in Tokyo, Japan.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.470
They have a completely different 
culture and civilization.

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:45.630
I guess there are a few 
cultural similarities.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.130
What is your name?

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:48.680
Hokaze Kon.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:49.550
All right, Kon.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:52.590
Tell me about your world.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.010
What?

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:58.910
A kid?

00:06:58.910 --> 00:06:59.850
Who are you?

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.350
Yodogawa Alan.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:02.960
I'm the Lab Chief.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.360
And I'm the president!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.860
Excuse me, can I please 
talk to someone in charge?

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.100
What's this little dude supposed to be?

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:12.090
You've got some nerve, 
fooling me like that.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.330
What's up with this prank?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:16.210
I'm telling you, I am the 
highest authority here.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.870
And I'm telling you that 
I don't believe you!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:18.620
Little brat!

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:22.630
Does a Hyperion judge others 
by their appearance?

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.620
This has nothing to do 
with being a Hyperion!

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:27.030
For people, appearance is like 120%.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:30.300
What's inside is just as unexplainable 
as complex compound math.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.000
I see.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.930
I guess that's to be 
expected from a Hyperion.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.400
As far as Alma power goes, 
the research is still pending

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.660
on the internal 
systems that control it.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.430
What is Alma, anyway?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:43.030
It's a fundamental energy 
found in all substances.

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:45.500
However, very few can actually 
utilize this energy.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.500
The Hyperion are some 
of the few that can.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.820
You did your homework, little boy.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.200
I keep telling you, I'm the Lab Chief.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:56.080
I guess you are dressed 
kinda like a scientist.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.460
So you're all complicated 
and deep, huh?

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.680
Then, take me to Olvidia.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.830
But Olvidia is not the 
world that you came from.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:08.020
Mitaka is not a sky-city and it's 
not an international city either.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.510
But I really feel like there is 
a way to get back in Olvidia.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:12.620
I see.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:13.550
Please!

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.090
You've doing research 
on Olvidia, right?

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.460
You know, it said "Ixion 
Research Center" outside,

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.640
but what's "Ixion", anyway?

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.140
I said we would be 
exchanging information.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.270
First I will inspect your body.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:30.500
My head tells me that 
this is for science,

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.650
but my body is getting 
really embarrassed.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.550
Pulse, blood pressure, 
and body temperature

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:38.300
seems the same as for normal humans.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.080
I mean, I'm nothing 
special, I know that.

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:45.660
Huh?

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:46.580
Isn't that the girl from before?

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:50.000
Commencing Experiment A-1.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:54.240
I'm down with cute nurses 
giving me an examination,

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.010
but don't you want to 
change into white first?

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.890
Do you find white 
uniforms more exciting?

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.310
You're a bad boy.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:08.520
Is this "Nani Kore Chin Hyakkei"?!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.820
Pulse, blood pressure, and body 
temperature have all risen.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:16.770
The (potential) Hyperion demonstrates 
the same response as any ordinary man.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:17.790
Hey!

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.330
You shouldn't be researching 
stuff like this, kid!

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.610
Make it stop!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.570
That was close.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.400
Get in the water, Kon.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.590
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.180
I should warn you.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.550
I don't think you're going 
to find anything special.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.730
Commencing Experiment A-2.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.200
Not that again.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.110
Can't we do something else?

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.050
What kind of fetish is this?

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:08.460
It looks like the (potential) 
Hyperion sinks, too.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.970
That was close!

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:15.760
All right. The next experiment.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.130
Stop right there!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.550
We're supposed to be 
exchanging information!

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.010
You did your experiments, 
now give me some information!

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.140
Your point is valid.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.470
You can ask me two questions.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.700
All right!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.900
How can I get to Olvidia?

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.450
I don't know.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:31.870
What do you mean, "I don't know"?

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.740
What if I got back on that airship I 
came on and just vroomed over there?

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:38.830
The airship can't fly high or fast 
enough to get you to Olvidia.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.990
Well, I guess that's it 
for your two questions.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:42.580
What?

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:43.280
Did I screw up?

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.700
Or is this guy just a prick?!

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:48.480
I simply applied the rules 
of information exchange.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:53.460
I answered your questions, 
so now it's my turn.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:55.300
I'm going to set up Experiment B-1.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.990
You trying to get one over on me?

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:01.890
Don't think you'll get away with it!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.020
1015, 1016, 1017...

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:12.990
Is something wrong?

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:22.780
I was wondering if this time, 
Kon will really go back to his world.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:24.120
Who knows?

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:26.570
I guess we'll have to see.

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:41.870
Make it stop!

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.510
The (potential) Hyperion 
is good at running away.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.860
No more!

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:04.350
Hey! Wait!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.620
<b>R15 
Self Regulation</b>

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.420
Stop! I'm calling off Experiment C-3.

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.610
That was really dangerous...

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:20.960
Let's take a short break.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.260
Then it's my turn to 
ask some questions!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.290
You get up to four.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:28.620
First off, what do you 
know about Olvidia?

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:30.220
Tell me everything.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.780
The (potential) Hyperion 
is exceedingly cunning.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:35.060
Make it clever or something.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.660
And stop saying "(potential)" already.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.730
I did it to be as precise 
as possible, but fine.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:43.490
It was starting to annoy me, too.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.740
All right. Now tell me.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.000
Based on visual data 
compiled from the ground,

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.370
this is what Olvidia might look like.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.780
Yeah, that's it!

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.230
I saw that for a second, too!

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.090
Then you were lucky.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.670
There is no regularity to 
Olvidia's observational data.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.670
We have no idea when 
and where it's flying.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:06.090
It's just floating around randomly?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.840
Or is someone... 
I was just talking to myself!

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.520
That wasn't a question!

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.000
Roughly 1,000 years ago...

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.480
You're going all the way back?

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.730
That was just some grumbling. 
It wasn't a question.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.540
In St. Piria's archival hall, 
there is one ancient document

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:24.390
of an eyewitness account.

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:27.080
But since then, each place 
has collected its own

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:31.240
myths, legends, and folklore 
alluding to the city in the sky.

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:34.030
They all explain it in their own way.

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:38.510
The indigenous people of what 
is now Jugglaburk's domain

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.550
called it "God's Castle" 
and believed that

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.600
the gods who created 
the world lived there.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.640
The people of the north 
however, believe that...

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.670
What I want to know, though, 
is what do you, as a scientist,

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:50.720
make of that place?

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:56.320
To float in the air like that, 
it must utilize some sort of energy.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.730
I speculate that it uses 
Alma as its power source.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:01.890
It means they have 
enough Alma Energy to

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:04.300
move something of that size
 and an efficient Alma engine.

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.580
I can't conclude that they are gods,

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:09.070
but I'm certain that it 
was built by someone.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.420
What do you mean, "someone"?

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:12.560
For what?

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.560
I don't know who.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:15.580
Nor do I know their objective.

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:17.360
Oh no!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:19.620
Your four questions are now over.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:20.750
I still have three!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.900
You asked me tell you my 
theory regarding Olvidia.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:26.640
Not what I know, but my theory.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:29.460
You wormed your way out of this one!

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.010
We'll resume the experiments.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.690
I'm so full.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.000
That was ordinary.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.510
I could eat more if this was
 conveyor belt sushi.

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:41.520
Conveyor belt sushi?

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:44.660
I could educate you, but it 
will cost you questions.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:45.650
Let's keep going.

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:52.360
It's done.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.900
Was I average? Better than? Below?

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:57.290
No, don't even tell me.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.180
I'll tell you.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:00.110
Below average.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:01.040
Shut up!

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:04.000
I'd like you to tell to me 
what you see in these images.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:08.140
The Dance Dance Revolution 
final match between the

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:12.060
volunteer soldiers fighting in the 
turf war between Mitaka and Nerima.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:13.260
And this?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.530
The mixed reaction of the 
kitchen staff that time when I

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.150
specifically went to a ramen 
place because it was recommended

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:19.140
by a magazine, which turned 
out to be so terrible that I

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.520
rushed into the kitchen demanding 
to make the ramen myself.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:23.740
The Hyperion lies.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:25.810
How do you know I'm lying?

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:27.190
That's not a question, by the way!

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.490
It's an objection!

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.780
You are so transparent.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.950
You're the one who keeps messing 
with me in the name of science!

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.780
I'm not getting any of 
the information I want!

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:38.160
You keep asking the wrong questions.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.300
And it looks like it's my 
turn to ask questions again!

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.790
Fine. You get two.

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:43.840
What are the top-secret facts

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:47.500
about Olvidia that you would 
never want me to know?

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:50.440
That's an interesting question.

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.760
I've solved quite a 
few quests in my day.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.840
An examination of the legends

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:58.030
has revealed the possibility 
of a mysterious route

00:15:58.030 --> 00:15:59.510
between the ground here and Olvidia.

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:03.430
However, the entrance on the 
ground has yet to be discovered.

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:05.540
Where do you think it is?

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.260
That was not a very good question.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:11.200
They've already searched all the places 
I thought might be a possibility.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.280
Yet they still can't find it.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.180
I told you in the very beginning

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.250
that I don't know how 
to get to Olvidia.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:20.250
I see.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.290
So even if you have a treasure trove 
of information about Olvidia,

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.780
you have no idea how to get there.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:28.090
And that's what you 
don't want to tell me.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.670
I've taken enough time here...

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.170
Can't you work with me more?

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.340
I want to know more about the Hyperion.

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:36.550
But there's nothing 
that I want to know.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:37.780
Wait!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.100
What the hell are you doing?

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:49.860
Don't go, big brother!

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:52.860
Oh god, is this supposed to be 
the adorable little brother?!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.610
You're all I have, big brother.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.790
But he's the one clinging 
to me, so am I

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.040
supposed to be the irresistible big brother?

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.870
Am I the one being adored here?

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:04.870
You're the only Hyperion 
test subject we have!

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:05.710
You're under...

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.830
...arrest.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:14.380
What the hell are you doing?!

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:16.600
Lemme go!

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.680
The Hyperion have the ability to collect

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.110
Alma Energy in their bodies 
and release it at will.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:23.680
Yeah? And?

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:26.030
Whether or not there is a 
specialized organ for this process

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:28.190
cannot be determined by 
mere hypothesis alone.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:39.090
To determine this, we will 
dissect the Hyperion.

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:41.040
Our aim is to find the Alma organ.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.360
Wait! Please wait!

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:44.370
There's no such thing!

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:47.170
But how can we know 
if we don't test it?

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:50.500
That's what x-rays and MRIs are for!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.750
You can do a non-invasive examination!

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:54.170
A response I'd expect from a Hyperion.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.810
They have technologies that we do not.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.130
Then let's begin.

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.640
We'll start with below the neck.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:05.320
Stop!

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:06.600
No!

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.560
Help!

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.220
What was that?

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.210
I'll go see.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:17.240
Kon! I'm here to get you out.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:24.620
This way's bad!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.660
In that case...

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:30.890
This way!

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:43.390
Don't run! Wait!

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:49.650
Even if we find something 
new, I'll never tell you!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.310
Big brother, I hate you!

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:58.870
Stop, stop, please stop!

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:01.950
Oh, I can't take it anymore!

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.240
It's so spicy! It burns!

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:08.040
What's going on?

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:11.540
We've been heavily reprimanded 
by headquarters.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.410
Reprimanded, I say! Reprimanded.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.360
I'm doing this to reflect 
and repent on my wrongs.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:21.050
What about you?

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:24.030
Well, we're under house arrest, 
which means we're stuck in this outpost.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:26.680
Which means I won't make 
my date with Akina-chan

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:29.670
when she gets off of work!

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:31.320
I can't make it to Moena-chan, either!

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:34.120
Damn, it's Anna-chan's birthday, too.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:35.960
Ah, I'm going to get a nose bleed!

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:37.830
I feel like I'm about 
to get a nose bleed!

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:39.820
And you?

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.700
Since I'm responsible 
for this situation,

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.190
I'm punishing myself by 
eating extremely spicy food.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:44.980
God, that's so hot!

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:47.860
You sickos.

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:49.150
I'm not a sicko.

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:52.240
I'm just really doing 
my best to endure it!

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.180
I am most definitely not a sicko!

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:56.130
This is self-criticism.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:57.420
I enduring it! So spicy!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.790
They're taking this very hard.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:12.230
Or so it seems.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.000
Erec-sama...

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:16.820
I guess this simply means 
that for us, Incognito,

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.780
action is all that we have.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:21.120
We have been punished long enough.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.780
We will now take action independently.

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:28.770
We will follow DT and infiltrate 
Jugglaburk's territory.

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:29.450
Yes, sir!

00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:35.990
Hurry up and make them stop that.

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:36.670
Yes, sir.

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:43.270
This is the first morning 
of the wedding rituals.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.360
The first ritual is a growing love.

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:49.660
The second ritual is an eternal love.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:51.900
The third ritual is a passionate love.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:53.090
The fourth...

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:54.680
Will you stand up straight?

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:56.920
You know, I've come 
to Jugglaburk's domain

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.870
and I still don't have a single lead.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.350
What did I even come here for?

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.200
You came for the princess's 
wedding rituals.

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:05.350
Should I go through all my intel again?

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.540
Or should I just start over?

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:12.200
And then, the eighteenth 
and last ritual, Olvidia.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:13.960
Olvidia?

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:16.440
What's the ritual about Olvidia?

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:19.550
You'll understand, once you 
reach the eighteenth ritual.

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:21.090
Can't you just tell me now?

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.420
No, I cannot. Those are the rules.

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:25.070
Back off, Kon.

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:26.020
You're being rude.

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:27.660
But he's talking about Olvidia,

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:30.450
the place I want to get to 
more than anything else!

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:32.570
Then why don't you just 
do your job properly

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:34.820
so I can complete the eighteen rituals?

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:36.410
Huh? Me?

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:39.110
It is custom that the eighteen rituals

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:42.380
are completed with the 
aid of the servants.

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:46.200
And now we will begin 
the wedding rituals.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.700
The first ritual is a growing love.

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:54.460
From here it's my turn.

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:58.260
Huh? That's all she has to do?

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:00.220
Afterwards, you just leave 
it to someone else?

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.620
It's a symbol.

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.840
Well, since I want to get to the 
last ritual as quickly as possible,

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:05.470
I guess that's good for me.

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.980
I'll take the craftsmanship part.

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:19.290
And the rider?

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:20.750
Kon, that'll be you.

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:21.380
Me?

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:22.730
What?

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:27.520
Help!

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:30.370
Why?!

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:33.410
Because it is tradition.

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:39.880
We're doing eighteen of these things?!

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:24.810
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:12.840
Ecarlate's wedding rituals have begun.

00:24:13.250 --> 00:24:15.580
Incognito's house arrest 
has yet to be lifted.

00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:19.640
However, we cannot just sit back and 
watch her get married to Jugglaburk.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:23.470
We're working on a secret 
plan to stop that wedding.

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:28.480
After being condemned to the 
sidelines for a long spell,

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:28.480
Incognito is finally striking back!

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:34.560
Meanwhile, Kon is enduring the 
hardships of the eighteen rituals.

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:34.560
Why is this necessary? 
Because it's a ritual.
